-- title:
--   Central twisted norm forces twisted conjugacy to a scalar (odd degree)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a finite-dimensional Galois extension of $K$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$), and assume the degree $n = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ is odd. Let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $b \in K^\times$, and write $\sigma$ also for the induced automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ obtained by applying $\sigma$ entrywise. The hypothesis is that the $\sigma$-twisted norm of $\delta$ of length $n$, namely the product $\delta\,\sigma(\delta)\,\sigma^2(\delta)\cdots\sigma^{n-1}(\delta)$ — formed by the recursion sending length $0$ to the identity and length $r+1$ to $\delta$ times $\sigma$ of the length-$r$ product — equals the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, under the entrywise structure map $K \to L$, of the scalar matrix $b\cdot 1$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$. The conclusion is that there exist $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $d \in L^\times$ with $h^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma(h) = d\cdot 1$, the scalar matrix with entry $d$.
--
--   In Langlands's analysis of $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy classes in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ for a cyclic extension $L/K$, the classes whose twisted norm is central and which are twisted-conjugate to a scalar are the classes of the first kind; the assertion here is that in odd degree every class with central norm coming from $K^\times$ is of this kind, the classes of the second kind (with twisted centraliser the unit group of a quaternion division algebra) occurring only in even degree. It is used in the comparison of the central contributions to the trace formula under cyclic base change, feeding into [`AutomorphicForm.setIntegral_sigmaCentralizerDomain_eq_mul_apply_centralScalar_of_normClassMap_eq_mk_scalar_of_central_transfer`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setIntegral_sigmaCentralizerDomain_eq_mul_apply_centralScalar_of_normClassMap_eq_mk_scalar_of_central_transfer), and it reduces via [`LT.TwistedNorm.exists_eq_sigmaConj_of_sigmaNormPow_eq_of_forall_mem_zpowers`](thm.html#LT.TwistedNorm.exists_eq_sigmaConj_of_sigmaNormPow_eq_of_forall_mem_zpowers) to exhibiting a scalar with the same twisted norm.
